<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Godfrey I of Louvain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1060–<a href="/years/1139">1139</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Godfrey the Bearded, Godfrey I of Brabant</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Godfrey I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuven">Louvain</a>, called the Bearded, was Count of Louvain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and, from 1106, Duke of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>. Although he later lost the ducal office, his family kept the title and became the dukes of Brabant. His daughter Adeliza married Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/godfrey-i-of-louvain.jpg" alt="Godfrey I of Louvain" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christophre Butkens,Abraham van Diepenbeeck,Mattheus Borrekens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Godffroy1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
